10
00:44:10,000 --> 00:44:16,000
Hail, Caesar!

11
00:48:35,000 --> 00:48:41,000
is a 2016 comedy mystery film written, produced, edited, and
directed by the brothers Joel and Ethan Coen.

12
00:53:00,000 --> 00:53:06,000
An American-British co-production, the film stars Josh Brolin, George Clooney, Alden Ehrenreich, Ralph Fiennes, Jonah Hill,
Scarlett Johansson, Frances McDormand, Tilda Swinton, and Channing Tatum, with Michael Gambon as the narrator.

13
00:57:25,000 --> 00:57:31,000
It is a fictional story that follows the real-life studio fixer Eddie Mannix (Brolin), working in the Hollywood film
industry in the 1950s, trying to discover what happened to a star actor during the filming of a biblical epic.

14
01:01:50,000 --> 01:01:56,000
First talked about by the Coens in 2004, Hail, Caesar!

15
01:06:15,000 --> 01:06:21,000
was originally to take place in the 1920s and follow
actors performing a play about ancient Rome.

16
01:10:40,000 --> 01:10:46,000
The Coens shelved the idea until late 2013.

17
01:15:05,000 --> 01:15:11,000
Principal photography for the film began in
November 2014 in Los Angeles, California.

18
01:19:30,000 --> 01:19:36,000
The film premiered at the Regency Village Theater in Los Angeles on February 1, 2016,
and was theatrically released by Universal Pictures on February 5.

19
01:23:55,000 --> 01:24:01,000
Hail, Caesar!

20
01:28:20,000 --> 01:28:26,000
grossed $63 million worldwide on a $22 million budget and
received positive reviews from critics.

21
01:32:45,000 --> 01:32:51,000
The film was chosen by National Board of Review as one of the top ten films of 2016, and received
Production Design nominations at the 89th Academy Awards and 70th British Academy Film Awards.

22
01:37:10,000 --> 01:37:16,000
The film explores themes of journalist, ransom, cat, kidnapping, ancient rome.

23
01:41:35,000 --> 01:41:41,000
The tone is lighthearted and emotional and mind_bending.
